WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.830
- Hey guys, it's Amy from Tasty UK.

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:04.230
And today I'm gonna be
trying the recipes of three

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.850
celebrities to decide who
makes the best avocado toast.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:08.990
In this mornings lineup,

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:11.530
we have cosmetic queen, Kylie Jenner,

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.960
the real queen of America, Meghan Markle,

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.660
and since we're talking royalty,

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.450
the potty mouth prince
himself, Gordon Ramsay.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.520
So who's gonna take the crown?

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.360
Let's find out.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.540
So we're gonna kick off
with Kylie Jenner's recipe.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:25.340
This one is relatively simple

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.490
and I am an avocado toast purist.

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:30.390
So you just slice your
two avocados in half.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:31.970
I'm just gonna score across the flesh

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:33.280
to make it easier to come out.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.660
So many people went to hospital
with avocado hand injuries

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.500
from removing the stone like that.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.810
So to safely remove the avocado stone,

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:42.600
you place a tea towel in your hand,

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.150
pop the avocado in there,

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:47.230
and confidently, viola.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:50.910
Kylie wants to show us that
she is a master of everything

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:53.010
and we've seen a lot of
her cooking on her socials.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:55.760
She's done Frosted flakes French toast,

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:56.680
which I actually made.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.180
And her French toast was banging.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:00:59.750
I have high expectations for this.

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:01.390
So I'm gonna scoop out the avocado flesh

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:02.840
and give it a mash in this bowl.

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:05.350
So you know your avo is ripe
when you pick off the stem

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:06.850
and beneath that you see green.

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:09.860
Avocado toast was a huge
thing a few years ago.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:13.300
Every cafe in East London worth its salt

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.920
has avo toast on the menu.

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:16.930
So this is looking really
nice and smooth now.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:17.990
So we're ready to plate.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:20.230
A great tip to stop your
avocado from browning,

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:21.800
if you're not quite ready to plate,

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:24.890
just pit a bit of cling wrap
on the surface of the avocado.

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:26.900
That way it cannot oxidize and go brown.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:28.760
So I'm gonna go ahead
and spoon this avocado

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:30.400
onto this lovely piece of toast.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.220
I'm gonna do a nice thick layer.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:35.830
A nice drizzle of agave.

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:37.000
A sprinkle of chili.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.370
And to finish, a bit of salt.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:40.300
And that is it.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.133
Wow.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:44.270
So this looks glistening and gorgeous.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.260
Look at that ratio of avo to bread.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:48.763
That is perfect.

00:01:50.541 --> 00:01:51.630
Mm.

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:52.530
I like it.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:55.900
It's very interesting
to put something sweet

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:57.340
on an avocado toast,

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:59.780
which isn't typically
something I would go for,

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:01.040
but I think the salt and the chili

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:02.270
is a really good addition.

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:03.960
I don't think this is an everyday thing.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:06.100
If you're looking for a
dessert avocado toast,

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.440
this is the way to go.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.580
But like I said, I'm a purist.

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:12.110
On a scale of one to
five, five being the best,

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:16.000
I'm giving Kylie Jenner's
avocado toast a 2.5.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.200
I don't hate it.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.010
That's a wrap on Kylie's recipe.

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:20.640
Let's see how Meghan measures up.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.090
I'm really excited about this one

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:26.430
because I think adding a
salty, cheesy feta-like element

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:28.290
is gonna really elevate this dish.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:29.900
We're gonna slice our avo in half.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:33.620
This recipe calls for one
avocado to two slices of toast.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:37.890
So it's a little bit stingy,
but maybe it's gonna be good.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.960
Again, with the avocado trick.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:40.950
Hey.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:42.020
We're gonna score this avo

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:44.960
just to make sure it's
easier to get out the skin.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:46.800
I heard that Meghan is a keen cook

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.780
and it's actually how
she snagged a prince.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:52.240
The story goes that Prince
Harry proposed to her

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.270
the day that she had
cooked her roast chicken.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:57.450
I have not myself tried or
seen any of Meghan's recipes,

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:59.830
but I can tell she's
got a taste for spice.

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:02.640
She's going around adding spice
to the royal family's lives.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:03.473
That's for sure.

00:03:03.473 --> 00:03:04.720
So we're just gonna scoop these avos out.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:07.140
We're gonna mash this avo
until it's nice and smooth.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:09.750
So I've half mashed this and
now I'm gonna add a tablespoon

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:12.050
of feta and then give it a good mix.

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:13.170
I'm using vegan feta,

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.800
but you can really use any that you like.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.650
I have high expectations for this one.

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:18.520
Salty, spicy, creamy.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:19.660
What's not to love?

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.810
I don't think this looks
the most visually appealing,

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:24.390
but I think the flavor
is gonna pack a punch.

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:26.240
So now we're gonna add some lemon juice.

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:27.970
Lemon juice makes everything better.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:28.897
I got it mostly in the bowl.

00:03:28.897 --> 00:03:31.400
And now I've added the lemon
juice, this is ready to plate.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.850
So for Meghan's recipe, we're
using multi-grain bread.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:36.190
And this is a bit of me,
I love this kind of bread.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:38.640
Pop this avocado on this bread.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.540
The bread to guac ratio is
not indulgent enough for me.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:43.980
It's gotta be 50 50.

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:45.050
This is flat.

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:47.160
I'm adding a little bit
more height and texture

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.460
with extra crumbles of feta.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:50.510
Gonna add some chili flakes.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:51.650
A bit of salt.

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:54.560
You can't have avo toast
that is unseasoned.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:56.870
And a few pepitas for crunch.

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:59.460
And there we go, Meghan
Markle's avocado toast.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:02.770
I'm trying to find an area
where there's some chunkiness

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:05.230
to this, and I know you
guys are gonna be mad,

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:08.793
but I'm gonna take a bite
out of the middle like this.

00:04:11.338 --> 00:04:12.171
Mm.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:15.030
There's a taste sensation.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:18.080
You know I was mad about the
ratios, but it actually works.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:19.720
And I think that's because of the feta.

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:22.050
You first get the creamy avocado layer.

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:25.780
And then you get these sort
of punches of salty cheese,

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:27.500
which is just delicious.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:28.920
And then on top of all of that,

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:31.170
you have the sprinkle of chili flakes,

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.560
which just makes this perfect.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:34.310
I got that all in one bite.

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:35.190
Well done Meghan.

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:39.630
I'm gonna give this avocado
toast a four out of five.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:40.463
I know.

00:04:40.463 --> 00:04:41.780
I'm just as surprised as you.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:43.230
This does really work.

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:44.163
So well done.

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:48.630
So now the one that I am
the most excited about.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:51.920
It is Chef Ramsay's avo toast.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:54.030
This next one is the
most chef-y of them all.

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:55.410
There are more steps in it.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:56.680
You actually have to do some cooking

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:57.940
rather than just assembly.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:58.960
Let's see if it's worth it.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:02.430
I'm gonna add some oil to
the pan and saute my chorizo.

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:04.680
I'm using vegan chorizo,
you can use any you like.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:06.710
I'm gonna cook this until
the edges are nice and crisp.

00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:08.440
And then we'll move on
to adding the onion.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:10.940
I think part of the
appeal of avocado toast

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:12.880
is how quick and simple it is to make.

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:13.713
But you know what?

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:15.190
I like the effort that he's gone to.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:18.130
He's put the Gordon Ramsay
spin on it and I'm into that.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:18.963
Ooh.

00:05:18.963 --> 00:05:20.890
So now the edges are
looking nice and crispy.

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:23.540
I'm gonna add the onion and
give that a little saute.

00:05:24.391 --> 00:05:25.780
Mm.

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:29.020
I haven't personally tried
Gordon's vegan recipes.

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:31.470
I feel like he said
something mean about vegans.

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:33.880
And since then we've not been friends.

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:35.630
So now that onion is nice and sauteed.

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:36.980
We're gonna add the garlic.

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:39.010
Just cook it until we can smell it

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:44.010
because there's nothing more
unforgivable than burnt garlic.

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:45.660
Unforgivable.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:47.100
That smells so good.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:51.600
I'm gonna make a gap in
the pan to add my tomatoes.

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.650
Tomatoes.
(crew laughs)

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:55.780
We have one cup.

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:58.470
So I'm going to add them cut side down

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:00.930
to the center of the pan
to give them a nice sear.

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:04.370
This is the most elaborate
avocado toast I've ever seen.

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:07.380
I could only make this recipe
after my first cup of coffee.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:11.850
But look, it looks like
some kind of child's art.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:13.870
It's like a preschool painting.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:16.570
The tomatoes are looking nice and sweaty.

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:18.540
We're just gonna wait until
they brown on the bottom

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:20.190
and then we'll deglaze the pan.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:22.430
Everyone loves Gordon Ramsay in England.

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:23.300
Is that true?

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:25.500
I mean, I can't speak
for the whole of England,

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:27.730
but Gordon Ramsay's a pretty liked guy.

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:30.160
I love Gordon Ramsay's duets.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.400
Gordon, if you're watching,

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:33.510
come at maybe with your duets on TikTok.

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:35.010
Check out my lasagna pie.

00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:36.850
The tomatoes are looking nice and charred.

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:39.500
So I'm gonna deglaze the pan
with some vegetable stock.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.000
The recipe calls for chicken stock,

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.250
but I'm using veggie today.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:44.790
It smells super fragrant, paprika-y,

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:47.530
garlicky, meaty.

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:48.950
Smells meaty.

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:51.620
It's looking very sophisticated.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:54.070
We've grown up, we've leveled up.

00:06:54.070 --> 00:06:55.320
So this is nice and reduced

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:56.970
and it smells gorgeous and juicy.

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:58.840
We're gonna add splash of sherry vinegar.

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:00.530
Give it a good season with salt.

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:01.363
And mix it up.

00:07:01.363 --> 00:07:02.300
A sprinkle of parley.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:04.310
So this was quite a lot of work,

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:06.110
but it's looking interesting.

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:08.610
I'm curious to see how this
is all gonna come together.

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:11.040
So we've got new components,
there's a lot going on here.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:12.620
So we're gonna take it step-by-step.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:13.760
Don't worry, I got you.

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:14.750
First of all, top tip,

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:16.490
we're gonna slice a piece of garlic

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:19.530
and rub the garlic on a
freshly toasted piece of bread,

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:21.640
just to add oomph to the flavor.

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:23.950
So we're using country
bread for this recipe,

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:25.670
a personal favorite of mine,

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:27.470
as of today when I learned what it was.

00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:29.960
Okay, so now it's finally avocado time.

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:30.920
So for this recipe,

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:33.520
I'm gonna slice the avocado
thinly and fan it out.

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:35.630
If you wanna find out how
to make an avocado rose,

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:37.457
I have a tutorial on my Instagram,

00:07:37.457 --> 00:07:38.950
@AmyTasty, check it out.

00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:41.960
I'm just gonna rub a bit
of olive oil over the top

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:44.930
of the avo just to make it nice and smooth

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:47.770
and as good looking as it can be.

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:49.360
And here we go with the slicing.

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:51.790
So half an avocado per piece of bread.

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:53.410
And just fan that out like so.

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:55.090
We're gonna season it with a bit of salt

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:56.280
and a squeeze of lemon.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:59.240
Next, the piece de resistance
is the chorizo mixture.

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:01.710
So I'm just gonna spoon
this over each piece,

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:04.250
giving it a nice generous layer.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:08.480
Mm, I love the tomatoes all smushed up.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:11.120
Pleasantly surprised by
the aesthetics of this.

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:13.640
Dressing these leaves
with a bit of olive oil.

00:08:13.640 --> 00:08:15.730
A touch of sherry vinegar.

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:16.990
And just a sprinkle of salt.

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:19.220
You know, I don't think I've
ever actually eaten avo toast

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:21.330
with lettuce, so this is quite uncommon.

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:23.720
I think this is kind
of getting far removed

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:26.550
from the essence that is avocado toast.

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:27.720
There's a lot going on here,

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:29.550
but what's most important
is how it tastes.

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:32.840
So let's add these leaves on
top, just for a bit of garnish,

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:35.460
bit of extra flavor, bit of extra crunch.

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:38.350
The final touches, we have
a sprinkle of parsley.

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:41.070
Finally, we have the manchego.

00:08:41.070 --> 00:08:42.120
I'm using vegan cheese.

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:43.410
You can use whatever cheese you like.

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:45.450
This seems like an unnecessary step.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:48.030
You've gone too far Gordon, but we'll see.

00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:49.720
I mean, he is a culinary genius.

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:51.670
So the ratios are wild here.

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:53.870
This is different from the other
recipes because rather than

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:57.280
a guacamole, it's a sliced
avocado, which I like,

00:08:57.280 --> 00:08:59.920
but then you've gone and
covered up those gorgeous slices

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:01.690
with all of these other elements.

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:03.560
The topping to bread ratio,

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:07.370
I'm a fan of because I like
a lot going on on the bread.

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:09.400
This is like lifting weights.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:10.840
Gonna get some guns.

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:12.073
So let's give it a go.

00:09:13.805 --> 00:09:15.448
Mm.

00:09:15.448 --> 00:09:16.281
Mm.

00:09:20.371 --> 00:09:21.690
Mm.

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:22.523
Yes Gordon.

00:09:22.523 --> 00:09:24.190
That is good.

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:26.550
Each individual layer comes through.

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:29.240
I would make this again,

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:31.970
but I wouldn't call this avocado toast.

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:35.260
This is chorizo's album,
avocado's just featuring on it.

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:37.290
I feel like the avocado kind of gets lost.

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:39.810
I think maybe the manchego was
supposed to give it a bit of

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:43.050
a salty edge, but you really
get that just from the chorizo.

00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:45.090
But this is a Sunday morning breakfast,

00:09:45.090 --> 00:09:46.220
when you've got a bit more time

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:48.160
to put a bit more energy and love into it.

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:50.190
So it's gonna come as
no surprise to anybody

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:52.865
that the chef is gonna make
the best avocado toast.

00:09:52.865 --> 00:09:55.540
I'm gonna give this a 4.5 out of five.

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:57.760
So congrats Gordon, you won.

00:09:57.760 --> 00:09:59.410
I'd suggest you make Gordon's recipe,

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:00.350
if you're feeling fancy

00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:02.190
and you've got a bit
more time on a Sunday.

00:10:02.190 --> 00:10:03.440
But I'd go for Meghan's,

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:05.840
if I was just making an
everyday avocado toast,

00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:08.590
because it's got that little
extra something special

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:10.320
without too much effort.

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:12.010
And if you're looking for something sweet,

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:13.430
sure, try Kylie's.

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:14.620
So that's it for me today.

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:16.700
If you have any other
celeb showdown ideas,

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:17.770
let us know in the comments.

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:18.770
Thanks for watching.

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:19.673
Bye.

00:10:19.673 --> 00:10:22.256
